From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KL7 <kl7@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:50:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kl7: do not wait for a missing IORTC during bsd_init

KL7 has no RTC node and nothing publishes an IORTC resource, so
IOKitInitializeTime() sleeps for the full 30-second waitForService()
timeout.  Skip the wait for SWEET; the calendar falls back to the epoch
until a real RTC driver exists.
---
 iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
@@ -77,9 +77,9 @@
 	t.tv_sec = 30;
 	t.tv_nsec = 0;
 
 // RTC is not present on this target
-#ifndef BCM2837
+#if !defined(BCM2837) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 	IOService::waitForService(
 		IOService::resourceMatching("IORTC"), &t );
 #endif
 #if defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
